    pr_ref:  # f4fa
    description: "**Defect.** 22 null-`shape_id` nodes are on structural kinds in real languages, contradicting the claim that null shape_ids only fall on non-structural kinds.\n\n**Mechanic.** The tree-sitter analyzers do not compute shape_id for several real-language structural-kind nodes, so those nodes are NULL even though they are class/function/method/interface/struct/enum — not the non-structural kinds null shape_ids were assumed to be confined to.\n\n**Scope.** Symbol shape_id field. shape_id_scheme=hypergumbo-shapeid-v2; 29862/34396 nodes have shape_id, 4534 NULL. Of those, 22 are real-language structural-kind nodes: csharp interface/method(x2)/class/enum/struct, solidity interface/function(x2), wgsl struct(x2)/function(x3), python function(x8) (route synthetics, kind=function with a `route` kind-slot, at serve.py:426-433). 7 of the 22 have BOTH stable_id and shape_id NULL (csharp class/struct/enum, solidity function x2, wgsl struct x2). csharp is among the spec's mainstream shape_id analyzers (§342-343) yet 0/6 csharp constructs get shape_id.\n\n**Expectation.** Structural-kind nodes in real languages would carry a shape_id, and any claim that null shape_ids fall only on non-structural kinds would hold.\n\n**Fix.** Compute shape_id for these structural-kind nodes across the affected tree-sitter analyzers; correct any documentation asserting null shape_ids are confined to non-structural kinds.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer using shape_id to cluster or track structural declarations silently drops these 22 class/function/method/interface/struct/enum nodes (7 of which have no identity hash at all beyond span-bearing id), and any documentation asserting null shape_ids are confined to non-structural kinds is false.\n\n**Cross-refs.** This corrects a prior characterization (the WI-ziguk ledger facet had described the null-shape_id nodes as confined to non-structural kinds). NOTE FOR OPERATOR: the tracker item WI-ziguk is status=wont_do and is about a different topic (validation_report undocumented in spec), so it was NOT auto-reopened; this shape_id structural-kind-null finding is filed as its own row. Adjacent to WI-rihob (container/declaration stable_id null) on the structural-identity-gap theme."  # f4fa
    fields: {}  # f4fa
